{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"group-phaseb","type":"group","x":5180,"y":136,"width":1520,"height":736,"label":"Phase B: Compiled Scheduler"},
		{"id":"group-phasea","type":"group","x":2110,"y":136,"width":2990,"height":260,"label":"Phase A: Modular Cleanup"},
		{"id":"group-guardr","type":"group","x":20,"y":136,"width":2010,"height":260,"label":"Guardrails"},
		{"id":"group-phasec","type":"group","x":5180,"y":992,"width":1030,"height":260,"label":"Phase C: Wire Thermal Reduction"},
		{"id":"8f691f4e","type":"text","text":"## PAM-01 P1-01 Add __slots__ to EDMState\nAdd slots=True to EDMState dataclass in core/state.py. Eliminates __dict__ lookup overhead on ~50+ attribute accesses per step. Expected: 0.5-1.5 us/step.","x":2170,"y":176,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"52cd1621","type":"text","text":"## GU-03 G-03 Dashboard refresh after each candidate\nUpdate performance_dashboard.html after each verified candidate. Ensures progress tracker stays current and sub-hotspot breakdown is visible for prioritizing the next cut.","x":1060,"y":176,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"4fced4b4","type":"text","text":"## GU-02 G-02 Fidelity lockstep check\nFor Phase 2 compiled path: run single-step comparison against modular reference path before the full 200k-step benchmark. Must match DEFAULT_FIDELITY_TOLERANCES (crater_count_abs=0, wire_temp_abs=0.5K, damage_abs=1e-4, position_abs=0.1um).","x":570,"y":176,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"1d21b3c5","type":"text","text":"## GU-01 G-01 Same-session reprofile gate\nEvery candidate must be profiled in the same session as the previous candidate to eliminate thermal/frequency drift. Use scripts/profile_simulation.py with same-session A/B workflow.","x":80,"y":176,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"canvas-errors","type":"text","text":"## Errors\n✓ None","x":-540,"y":-750,"width":380,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"legend","type":"text","text":"## Legend\n🔴 **Red** = To Do (ready)\n⬜ **Gray** = Blocked\n🟠 **Orange** = Doing\n🔵 **Cyan** = Ready to review\n🟢 **Green** = Done\n🟣 **Purple** = Proposed by agent","x":-540,"y":-310,"width":380,"height":230,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"canvas-warnings","type":"text","text":"## Warnings\n✓ None","x":-540,"y":-530,"width":380,"height":200,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"b9f45f24","type":"text","text":"## PBC-02 P2-02 Compiled @njit inner loop\nCompiled scheduler fixed for control-state sync and mode-dependent crater geometry. Validation: 112 pytest tests pass including 21 compiled-path tests. Reproducible bench_compiled.py shows real but smaller gains: about 1.40x at 0.20 mm and 1.30x at 0.05 mm on 200k repeated runs; 1M one-off A/B was about 1.20x and 1.17x. Fidelity is aligned within test/profile tolerances, not exact bitwise parity.","x":5240,"y":652,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"b2a562df","type":"text","text":"## PBC-01 P2-01 Flat numeric hot-state bundle\nDefine pure-numeric state representation for ~30 scalars + 4 wire arrays. spark_status as 3 numeric scalars with NaN sentinel. No Python objects in hot path. EDMState remains public API.","x":5240,"y":176,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"c16b0fb2","type":"text","text":"## PAM-07 P1-05 Drop convection-boundary idea for 1 us benchmark\nCurrent realtime contract uses servo_interval == dt == 1 us, so updating convection only at control boundaries is still every microstep and is not a meaningful optimization. Replace PAM-05 with PAM-06 or another measured Phase A win instead of pursuing this card.","x":4620,"y":176,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"7e3b7897","type":"text","text":"## PBC-03 Branch-consistent RNG architecture\nAttempted staged RNG/discharge/finalize split. Initial fastmath finalize kernel broke fidelity via NaN flow-condition handling; removing fastmath restored parity, but same-session 1M A/B still favored legacy PBC-04 by 14.7 pct on the coarse mesh and 6.0 pct on the fine mesh. Reverted the public compiled path to the simpler PBC-04 implementation and kept only the RNG-parity regression test plus documentation of the non-win.","x":5730,"y":652,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"b4fff437","type":"text","text":"## PBC-05 PBC-05 Numeric action packet + compiled env bookkeeping\nImplemented a pre-resolved CompiledActionPacket in src/wedm/envs/wire_edm.py, cached immutable ScalarAction inputs for repeated compiled stepping, folded compiled termination status into src/wedm/core/compiled_step.py, and updated the profiling/bench scripts to precompile the action once per env run. Validation: python -m pytest -q -> 124 passed. Official uncontended candidate perf_candidate_compiled_20260401_152709.json verified PASS at 213389.81 steps/s (0.20 mm) and 158583.94 steps/s (0.05 mm), which is +3.69 over the best verified PBC-04 candidate. 1M A/B: 180709.05->226510.81 and 136429.79->168103.65. Details: docs/realtime_optimization_execution_results.md.","x":6220,"y":652,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"f0760043","type":"text","text":"## PBC-04  Tighten step() fast path\nImplemented step_fast()/step_compiled_fast() and compiled mode caching; profile_simulation.py and bench_compiled.py now prefer fast paths. Validation: 120 tests pass. Candidate perf_candidate_compiled_20260330_014515 hit 205800 / 154805 steps/s at 200k with PASS fidelity. 1M A/B: 159335->217061 (1.362x) and 131774->153622 (1.166x).","x":6220,"y":176,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"812165b7","type":"text","text":"## PAM-06 P1-05r Slots on module param dataclasses\nExperiment evaluated and reverted: slots on module parameter dataclasses showed no steady-state gain and added rigidity. Findings: docs/realtime_optimization_non_wins.md.","x":4130,"y":176,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"8c990064","type":"text","text":"## PAM-04 P1-04 Non-Optional voltage/current\nChanged EDMState voltage/current defaults to 0.0 and removed hot-path None checks; 1M-step fidelity PASS, measured plus 0.7 percent at 0.20 mm and minus 0.1 percent at 0.05 mm. Details: docs/realtime_optimization_execution_results.md.","x":3640,"y":176,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"fca6958a","type":"text","text":"## PAM-03 P1-03 Remove redundant float() casts\nImplemented cast cleanup in ignition/wire; 1M-step fidelity PASS, measured plus 6.8 percent at 0.20 mm and plus 12.9 percent at 0.05 mm. Details: docs/realtime_optimization_execution_results.md.","x":3150,"y":176,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"1160ff9f","type":"text","text":"## PAM-02 P1-02 Scalar RNG in ignition\nReplace np_random.random(2) array alloc in ignition.py:581 with two scalar np_random.random() calls. Avoids per-step array allocation and float boxing. Expected: 0.5-1.0 us/step.","x":2660,"y":176,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"bb7eab4e","type":"text","text":"## GU-04 Compiled wire sub-bucket visibility\nImplemented profiling-only compiled wire sub-bucket visibility without changing the production fast path. The compiled hotspot pass now populates module_subhotspots.wire in the profiling JSON and dashboard. Validation: python -m pytest -q -> 125 passed. Latest dashboard-backed report perf_candidate_compiled_20260401_170508.json now shows compiled wire sub-buckets: coarse thermal_core 18.96, damage 12.41; fine damage 18.84, discharge_partition 6.26. This was an observability task only, not a speed optimization. Details: docs/realtime_optimization_execution_results.md.","x":1550,"y":176,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"998f9e77","type":"text","text":"## PBC-06 Constant-action compiled loop\nAdd a benchmark/training-oriented compiled loop that advances many microsteps under one already-resolved action packet, reducing the remaining Python call overhead without changing physics or the public step API. Keep this as an additional fast path rather than rewriting the default API. Validate separately from the normal per-step path and document where it is appropriate to use it.","x":5730,"y":176,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"aa06438b","type":"text","text":"## PCW-02 P3-02 SIMD-friendly loop restructuring\nAttempted split-pass wire thermal kernel (derivative/update/damage) inside src/wedm/modules/wire.py. Result: conservative-track non-win. Candidate verification failed fidelity on mean wire temperature: 0.20 mm 312.30 K -> 296.82 K at 81346.49 steps/s, 0.05 mm 312.30 K -> 296.86 K at 52975.43 steps/s, while crater count and workpiece position stayed aligned. Restored the original interleaved kernel path, reran targeted validation (38 passed), and confirmed the shipped compiled path returns to PASS fidelity at 104877.66 / 76622.92 steps/s. Findings documented in docs/realtime_optimization_execution_results.md and docs/realtime_optimization_non_wins.md.","x":5730,"y":1032,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"7cf2c66b","type":"text","text":"## PCW-01 P3-01 Active thermal window\nCompute full conduction-convection-damage only for segments near spark/contacts (+-5-10 segs). Cold tails updated every 100-500us. Reduces wire from O(N) to O(W) where W<<N. Expected: 7-50x wire reduction.","x":5240,"y":1032,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"6"}
	],
